abstract: >-
  MIRR is a safety-critical domain-specific language compiler that transforms
  temporal behavioral specifications into synthesizable SystemVerilog RTL,
  FIRRTL, R-SPU assembly, S-expression IR, and SystemVerilog Assertions (SVA).
  The compiler uses a hand-rolled Entity Component System (ECS) as its IR,
  eliminating pointer-chained AST traversal in favour of cache-local flat Vec
  arrays. Temporal guard semantics compile to deterministic shift-register chains
  in hardware. The project follows NASA Power-of-10 coding rules, enforces zero
  unsafe code across all crates, and includes 80+ formal Rocq proofs covering
  width inference and temporal guard correctness.
